OL,3,CKing plants royal rose as he begins
OL,4,Csummer break in Scotland
OL,6,FThe King has begun his summer break in
OL,7,FScotland by planting a royal rose at
OL,8,Fthe Castle and Gardens of Mey in
OL,9,FCaithness.
OL,11,FCharles spends the first week of
OL,12,FAugust at the castle every year,
OL,13,Fcoinciding with the birthday of his
OL,14,Fgrandmother, the late Queen Mother.
OL,16,FDuring his time at the castle, Charles
OL,17,Fplanted the King's Rose, which was
OL,18,Fcultivated by David Austin Roses in
OL,19,Fpartnership with The King's Foundation
OL,20,Fand named in his honour, in the
OL,21,Fcastle's Diamond Jubilee Rose Garden.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G1/3
